    36	
    37	- **Most explicit modern statement opened:** Robert Theodore Williams Jr., *Commutator Formulas in Groups of Kac-Moody Type*, thesis, August 2022, DOI [10.18130/t9v1-vz61](https://doi.org/10.18130/t9v1-vz61), printed p.49 / PDF p.55, after Definition 6.1.5: “They coincide in (at least) the case that A is a symmetrizable matrix … but it is not known if they always coincide or if there is a GCM A for which they do not.” The preceding text explicitly identifies the two quotients. Full PDF opened and saved as `sources/williams-thesis-2022.pdf`; text lines 2079–2098.
    38	- **Later fresh discussion:** Timothée Marquis, [arXiv:2309.02508](https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.02508), September 5, 2023, §6.2 “Open questions”, p.11: for characteristic zero and A not necessarily symmetrizable, the group GK-simplicity question is equivalent to proving the Gabber–Kac theorem for A. The notes use the Serre-defined algebra and state that theorem only for symmetrizable A. This is the equivalent open formulation, not a positive-characteristic counterexample.
