    66	
    67	## Attack
    68	
    69	### Exact algorithm and proof of its meaning
    70	
    71	[`proof.md`](proof.md) proves, without assuming the conjecture, that the positive maximal ideal is obtained recursively by
    72	
    73	    K_ei=0,
    74	    K_alpha={x in L_alpha : D_i x in K_(alpha-ei) for all i}.
    75	
    76	It also proves the exact Serre-ideal recurrence from the original generators plus [e_i,I_(alpha-ei)]. Thus dim L_alpha/I_alpha and dim L_alpha/K_alpha are genuinely different constructions being compared, not two labels for one quotient. The code does not use a symmetrizable root-multiplicity formula for a nonsymmetrizable input.
    77	
    78	The producer, [`work/graded_lie.py`](work/graded_lie.py), uses recursive bracket lowering. The separate checker, [`work/check_certificate.py`](work/check_certificate.py), imports no producer code and computes lowering by an independently derived associative-word deletion formula, followed by independently reconstructed coordinates. It regenerates exact Serre spans and checks injectivity on their quotients, which proves I=K inductively; a nonzero-defect certificate is explicitly refused rather than mislabeled an equality pass. The height, matrix set, and entries are bound to an external requested scope and fixed specification. Six negative controls test field, missing degree, changed dimension, omitted matrix, altered matrix, and height. A finite-field rank match alone is not the accepted evidence; the exact-Q certificate and independent checker are the acceptance path.
    79	
    80	### Proved infinite boundary family
    81	
    82	**If deleting one index i leaves a symmetrizable principal GCM, then I_alpha=K_alpha in every degree with alpha_i=1.** The proof constructs a symmetrizable comparison matrix preserving the entire coefficient-one Serre slice and every complementary lowering, then uses its nondegenerate opposite-root pairing. It does not assume the full nonsymmetrizable algebra has an invariant symmetric form.
    83	
    84	For rank three this excludes **every** degree with a zero or one coordinate, at all heights. The structural proof alone gives equality through height five and leaves (2,2,2) as the first candidate. The separate symbolic certificate below excludes that candidate uniformly as well, proving equality through height six for every rank-three GCM. An independently derived all-(m,1,1) calculation and the full coefficient-one proof are preserved in [`evidence/descent-audit.md`](evidence/descent-audit.md). These are bounded or boundary results; novelty has not been established.
    85	
    86	A first extra relation must also be annihilated by every lowering. Integrable sl2 theory then gives the necessary condition A alpha<=0. This directs the remaining attack to interior imaginary degrees, not already-excluded boundary degrees.
    87	
    88	### Bounded exact computations
    89	
    90	The three genuinely nonsymmetrizable input matrices are
    91	
    92	    A_one   = [[2,-1,-1],[-1,2,-1],[-2,-1,2]],
    93	    A_cycle = [[2,-1,-2],[-2,2,-1],[-1,-2,2]],
    94	    A_large = [[2,-2,-2],[-3,2,-2],[-2,-3,2]].
    95	
    96	Their absolute directed cycle products are respectively 2 vs 1, 1 vs 8, and 8 vs 18, excluding a diagonal symmetrizer.
    97	
    98	The exact-Q computations and independent scope-bound checks passed: **no discrepancy in any positive multidegree through height 10** for all three matrices and the A3 / affine-A2 controls (258 nonzero free-Lie degrees per matrix; 1,290 checked matrix-degree records), and through height 12 for A_one (421 degree records). All other positive degrees in those ranges have zero free-Lie dimension. Each check rejected all six negative controls. These are bounded results, not the full theorem.
    99	
   100	| Matrix | dim at (2,2,2), both quotients | dim at (3,3,3), both quotients |
   101	|---|---:|---:|
   102	| A_one | 3 | 8 |
   103	| A_cycle | 5 | 31 |
   104	| A_large | 14 | 148 |
   105	| affine-A2 control | 2 | 2 |
   106	
   107	The free-Lie dimensions at those degrees are 14 and 186. The samples include interior weights in A alpha<=0, so the computation is not just rechecking the boundary theorem. Evidence: [`evidence/interior-root-samples.json`](evidence/interior-root-samples.json), [`height-10 independent PASS`](evidence/rational-height10/independent-check.json), and [`height-12 independent PASS`](evidence/rational-height12/independent-check.json), with full certificates and source/scope hashes. The two earlier unbound checker runs were cancelled without acceptance; they are not counted.
   108	
   109	### Uniform symbolic interior theorem and failed routes
   110	
   111	**Every rank-three GCM has I_alpha=K_alpha through total height six.** After the coefficient-one theorem, only (2,2,2) remained. For strictly negative off-diagonals, partition their six magnitudes into 1 versus 2+x, x>=0. This creates 64 cells covering arbitrarily large entries. Through componentwise degree (2,2,2), Serre ideal spaces depend only on the cell, while each lowering matrix is affine in its free parameters.
   112	
   113	The producer found positive-coefficient maximal-minor certificates in 58 cells; the first chosen minor was inconclusive in six. **The six failures were not dropped.** Exact simultaneous index permutations map every cell to one of 16 successful representatives, and degree (2,2,2) is permutation-invariant. The independent checker reconstructed all representative matrices, verified the full determinant identities by fraction-free Bareiss elimination in FLINT, checked positivity including the constant term, and verified complete 64-cell coverage. Matrices with a zero off-diagonal pair are symmetrizable in rank three and are handled separately.
   114	
   115	The complete logical bridge is [`proof.md` §9](proof.md), with [`all-cell independent PASS`](evidence/symbolic-222/all-cells-independent-check.json) and [`permutation coverage`](evidence/symbolic-222/permutation-cover.json). For the largest representative, a 14-by-14 minor has 3,699 positive terms, constant 286654464, and total degree 14. These are exact polynomial identities, not evaluations at finitely many matrices. The first rank-three degrees not excluded **uniformly** now have height at least seven. No all-height nonsymmetrizable case or novelty claim follows.
   116	
   117	The initial SymPy reporting exception is preserved in `evidence/symbolic-222-first-attempt.json`. The direct all-cell checker correctly rejected mask 1 before symmetry coverage was supplied; its stricter predecessor is preserved as `evidence/check_interior_cells-direct.py`. The final proof changes the argument by a verified symmetry reduction, not by weakening the required parameter coverage.
   118	
   119	No all-height reduction of interior degrees was found. The standard invariant-form route cannot simply be applied to the original nonsymmetrizable A. Even the coefficient-one comparison breaks at coefficient two: altered i-row Serre relations and i-lowerings can then matter. Finite exact agreement, modular agreement, and the known symmetrizable theorem do not close that gap.
