   166	
   167	## Next steps
   168	
   169	The full goal remains J=tau for every GCM. The precise next analytic step is to control the **interior** lowest-weight vectors, where the symmetrizable comparison no longer intertwines the missing lowering. For A_one, the necessary conditions alpha_i>=2 and A_one alpha<=0 leave only **(4,4,5)** at height 13 after the bounded height-12 computation; at height 14 they leave only (4,4,6). This is a candidate for investigation, not a claimed defect. See [`evidence/next-interior-degrees.json`](evidence/next-interior-degrees.json).
   170	
   171	A useful route is to decompose these levels under the symmetrizable rank-two Levi and analyze the remaining f_i coupling on its lowest-weight vectors, rather than infer a global theorem from longer numerical searches. Any proposed all-height argument must explain why no first extra relation can appear at an arbitrarily large interior degree. If a candidate defect is found, supply its exact rational Lie polynomial, verify its nonmembership in the Serre ideal and every required descent, and run the independent checker before calling it a counterexample.

