   161	## 9. Computer-assisted theorem: every rank-three GCM agrees through height six
   162	
   163	**Theorem.** For every rank-three GCM in characteristic zero, I_alpha=K_alpha for every positive alpha of total height at most six. In particular no additional defining relation can first occur below height seven in rank three. This is a bounded-height theorem for an unbounded family of matrices, not an all-height theorem for any nonsymmetrizable matrix. Its novelty in the literature has not been established.
   164	
   165	**Proof.** Section 7 handles every degree with a coordinate zero or one. The only remaining positive degree of height at most six is alpha=(2,2,2). If some off-diagonal pair is zero, the underlying graph on three vertices is a forest and A is symmetrizable: choose positive diagonal ratios along its edges, independently on components. Gabber–Kac then applies.
   166	
   167	Assume all six off-diagonal entries are strictly negative. Order their magnitudes by the edges
   168	
   169	    (1,2), (1,3), (2,1), (2,3), (3,1), (3,2).
   170	
   171	For each magnitude, either it is 1 or it is 2+x with x a nonnegative integer. These choices partition every such GCM into 64 cells. A mask bit equal to one denotes the fixed magnitude 1; a zero bit denotes 2+x. There is no upper bound on x.
   172	
   173	In all degrees beta componentwise at most (2,2,2), the positive Serre ideal depends only on the mask, not on the free parameters. A relation for magnitude 1 is (ad e_i)^2 e_j and can contribute; for magnitude at least 2 it contains at least three e_i and cannot contribute in these degrees or to them by positive ideal generation. The ideal projections are therefore fixed rational linear maps within each cell.
   174	
   175	The joint lowering from L_222/I_222 to the three immediate lower quotients has an affine-linear rational matrix M(x): one application of ad(f_i) is linear in the Cartan entries, and the source/target ideal projections are constant. The lower degrees (1,2,2), (2,1,2), (2,2,1) are coefficient-one degrees, so Section 7 already identifies their Serre and maximal quotients. Consequently injectivity of M(x) proves I_222=K_222.
   176	
   177	The certificate supplies a maximal square minor and its exact determinant polynomial for each of 16 representative masks:
   178	
   179	    0,2,3,5,6,7,10,11,15,22,23,25,27,30,31,63.
   180	
   181	For each representative, after a recorded overall sign, every nonzero coefficient of its determinant is positive rational and its constant coefficient is strictly positive. Hence the determinant is positive whenever all free parameters are nonnegative. Each selected minor is therefore nonzero, proving injectivity on that entire parameter cell, not merely at sampled matrices.
   182	
   183	`evidence/symbolic-222/permutation-cover.json` supplies, for **each of all 64 masks**, a permutation of the three indices taking it to one of these representative cells. The independent checker verifies every permutation and mask transformation and rejects an omitted cell. Simultaneously permuting e_i, f_i, h_i and the rows/columns of A preserves both ideal constructions, and the degree (2,2,2) is fixed by every such permutation. Therefore the representative certificates cover every cell.
   184	
   185	The independent verification is `work/check_interior_cells.py`, with receipt `evidence/symbolic-222/all-cells-independent-check.json`. It does not import the producer or SymPy. It reconstructs the exact Serre ideal spaces and the lowering matrices using the independently derived tensor-word formula, checks every saved affine entry, clears denominators, and computes each determinant by explicit fraction-free Bareiss elimination over FLINT's integer multivariate polynomial ring. Every division is checked to have zero remainder, and the full polynomial coefficient list is compared exactly. Sixteen altered determinant coefficients and an omitted coverage cell are rejected. The receipt binds every representative certificate and the coverage file by SHA-256.
   186	
   187	For example, mask 0 (all magnitudes at least 2) has a 14-by-14 minor. Its sign-normalized determinant has 3,699 positive terms, constant 286654464, and total degree 14; the separate `independent-check.json` in that directory verifies it. The other representatives have smaller minors. The proof depends on the full checked identities, not this example or floating-point evaluations. This establishes injectivity in every cell, completing the theorem. QED.
   188	
   189	**Failed route preserved.** The first lexicographic minor was not coefficientwise positive in six masks (1,17,21,33,37,49). This is not a counterexample to injectivity. The direct 64-positive-minor checker correctly rejected that incomplete argument. The final proof does not suppress those failures: it replaces their minors by explicitly verified index permutations to successful representatives, with complete coverage still required. The initial reporting exception and the direct-check rejection are retained in evidence.
   190	
   191	## 10. Remaining mathematical gap
   192	
   193	Agreement at finite height does not imply I=K in all heights. The recurrence constructs an exact search for a first additional relation, but supplies no uniform bound on where a first relation would occur if one exists. A proof of the book conjecture requires an all-height argument for every nonsymmetrizable GCM, not three matrices and not a finite-dimensional truncation. Conversely a modular discrepancy needs exact characteristic-zero confirmation and explicit witness verification before it can be called a counterexample.

