codex
**READY** for the Section 9 height-six theorem. I found no mathematical or checker error requiring repair.

- **Exhaustiveness is sound.** Section 7 leaves only degree (2,2,2). A zero off-diagonal pair makes the three-vertex graph a forest, hence symmetrizable. Otherwise, six independent choices of magnitude 1 versus 2+x partition every strictly negative GCM into exactly 64 unbounded cells. [proof.md §9](/Users/jinleic/jinleic-workspace/ai4s/kac-moody-serre-relations/proof.md:165)

- **Serre spans are constant, and parameter dependence is genuinely affine.** Generators with magnitude ≥2 contain ≥3 copies of their leading letter; positive ideal generation cannot bring them into the componentwise box ≤222. The checker reconstructs the remaining generators and their bracket closure. Fixed rational quotient projections and linear word-deletion lowering justify recovering every affine coefficient from the baseline and individual shifts. These evaluations determine an already-proved affine map. [Serre reconstruction](/Users/jinleic/jinleic-workspace/ai4s/kac-moody-serre-relations/work/check_interior_cells.py:64)

